This repository contains installers and verifiers only. It does not
redistribute the Graphify skill or the graphifyy Python package.

At install time, the installer downloads the skill from the upstream
repository:

  https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify
  (the upstream README also references https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify)

The default ref is `main`, which is the branch that still contains the
single-file skill this project adapts:

  skills/graphify/skill.md

That branch declares MIT in pyproject.toml:

  license = { text = "MIT" }

The `main` branch has no standalone LICENSE file, so the full MIT text is not
available from that branch.

Upstream's current default branch (v8) has a different layout and licensing:
Apache-2.0 in LICENSE, with pre-relicensing contributions under MIT in
LICENSE-MIT and attribution in NOTICE. The graphifyy package is installed
separately from PyPI; the 0.9.119 release reports
License-Expression: Apache-2.0.

Graphify is maintained upstream by Graphify Labs. LICENSE-MIT credits Safi
Shamsi and the Graphify contributors. This project is unofficial and is not
affiliated with the upstream authors.
